            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0357" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">870.811/49</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Swiss Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jenny</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic">August 10,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Department of</seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">German Interests</seg>
                    <lb/>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">XXXIV Pr.</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By direction of my Government, I have the
                    honor, herewith, to transmit to your Excellency the transcript of a cable from
                    the Swiss Foreign Office concerning protest of the German Government against the
                    nomination by the United States of the American citizen, Mr. Hines, as
                    Arbitrator according to Article 339 of the Peace Treaty of Versailles.</p>
                <p>I am also instructed to add that the German Government has always desired that
                    normal relations with the United States be reestablished, but that it can take
                    another position in the present case only after such normal relations have been
                    re-established.</p>
                <p>I shall be happy to transmit to the Swiss Foreign Office, for communication to
                    the German Government, any reply your Excellency may desire to make in the
                    premises.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>Dr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Jenny</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d222-a1.xml" xpointer="d222-a1"/>
            </div>
